Subject: server,winemac.drv: RawInput active-window fallback and IME non-output passthrough

1. In server/queue.c find_hardware_message_window(), fall back from
   input_shm->focus to input_shm->active for QS_RAWINPUT when msg->win == 0,
   matching get_foreground_thread() and QS_KEY.
2. In winemac.drv macdrv_ime_process_key(), only consume a key event as
   VK_PROCESSKEY when Cocoa inputContext actually produced text/markedText
   output or was acting on existing markedText, preventing non-composing
   control keys (Return, Space, etc.) or IMK hiccups from being eaten.

diff --git a/server/queue.c b/server/queue.c
index 9e22a4a..ec1c6a4 100644
--- a/server/queue.c
+++ b/server/queue.c
@@ -1909,10 +1909,15 @@ static user_handle_t find_hardware_message_window( struct desktop *desktop, stru
     switch (get_hardware_msg_bit( msg->msg ))
     {
     case QS_POINTER:
-    case QS_RAWINPUT:
     case QS_HARDWARE:
         if (!(win = msg->win) && input) win = input_shm->focus;
         break;
+    case QS_RAWINPUT:
+        if (!(win = msg->win) && input)
+        {
+            if (!(win = input_shm->focus)) win = input_shm->active;
+        }
+        break;
     case QS_KEY:
         if (input && !(win = input_shm->focus))
         {
